  "reasoning": "The defendants, who were village cadres, used false personal information and public land to fraudulently obtain loss‑land farmer pension insurance for themselves and relatives, collecting large cash payments under the pretense of processing fees. This constitutes fraud to obtain social security benefits, i.e., a fraud (诈骗) offense. No other distinct crimes such as bribery or embezzlement are evident beyond the fraudulent acquisition of the insurance benefits.",
